[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Compound Queries, Bool Logic, and Scoring in Elasticsearch"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Elasticsearch provides robust mechanisms to combine multiple search criteria using compound queries. At the heart of this functionality is the bool query, which allows developers to construct complex boolean logic and influence document relevance scoring."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Understanding the Bool Query Structure"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"The bool query takes a segmented approach to combining queries by breaking them down into four core clauses. Each clause serves a distinct purpose in matching documents and calculating scores."},{"order":5,"type":"bullet_point","text":"must: The clause (query) must appear in matching documents and will contribute to the relevance score."},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"filter: The clause (query) must appear in matching documents. However, unlike 'must', the score of the query is ignored, and clauses are executed in filter context for caching optimization."},{"order":7,"type":"bullet_point","text":"should: The clause (query) should appear in the matching document. In a query context, it adds to the relevance score."},{"order":8,"type":"bullet_point","text":"must_not: The clause (query) must not appear in the matching documents. Executed in filter context, scores are ignored."},{"order":9,"type":"subheading","text":"Practical Implementation"},{"order":10,"type":"paragraph","text":"Consider an e-commerce search scenario where we want to find products that match a specific text search, fall within a price range, and exclude out-of-stock items."},{"order":11,"type":"code","text":"POST /products/_search
{
  "query": {
    "bool": {
      "must": [
        { "match": { "name": "wireless headphones" } }
      ],
      "filter": [
        { "range": { "price": { "gte": 50, "lte": 200 } } }
      ],
      "must_not": [
        { "term": { "status": "discontinued" } }
      ],
      "should": [
        { "term": { "brand.keyword": "AudioTech" } }
      ],
      "minimum_should_match": 0
    }
  }
}"},{"order":12,"type":"subheading","text":"Scoring Dynamics and Contexts"},{"order":13,"type":"paragraph","text":"Elasticsearch evaluates queries in two distinct contexts: query context and filter context. Understanding how scoring behaves in each context is crucial for performance and search precision."},{"order":14,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Query Context: Determines how well each document matches the query, calculating a relevance score (_score) assigned to the '_score' metadata field."},{"order":15,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Filter Context: Asks a binary yes/no question about whether a document matches. These results are heavily cached by Elasticsearch automatically, making them ideal for exact matches, ranges, and status flags."},{"order":16,"type":"subheading","text":"Controlling the Score with minimum_should_match"},{"order":17,"type":"paragraph","text":"When using 'should' clauses outside of a 'must' clause, Elasticsearch does not require them to match by default. You can enforce a threshold using the 'minimum_should_match' parameter to ensure that a specific number or percentage of 'should' clauses match for a document to be returned."}]
